    {
      "n": 17,
      "title": "6.What are the parameters measured by spirometry? (mobilizable volumes)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "6.What are the parameters measured by spirometry? (mobilizable volumes)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 18,
      "title": "the fraction of vital capacity (CV) expired in 1 second by rapid, forced expiration.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "6.What are the parameters measured by spirometry? (mobilizable volumes)"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Vital capacity (CV): volume of air mobilized by a"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "forced expiration following forced inspiration."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The maximum expiratory volume / second (FEV): this is"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "the fraction of vital capacity (CV) expired in 1 second by rapid, forced expiration."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 19,
      "title": "? The FEV/CV ratio determines the Tiffeneau index (TI)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "6.What are the parameters measured by spirometry? (mobilizable volumes)"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Vital capacity (CV): volume of air mobilized by"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "a forced expiration following a forced inspiration."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The maximum expiratory volume/second (FEV): it is the fraction of the vital capacity (CV) expired in 1 second by rapid and forced expiration."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "? The FEV/CV ratio determines the Tiffeneau index (TI)"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Peripheral flow rates"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "normalized: flow rates normalized to a percentage of CV measured at a point on the forced expiration curve."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 20,
      "title": "7.Define non-mobilizable volumes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "7.Define non-mobilizable volumes"
