    },
    {
      "n": 21,
      "title": "7.Define non-mobilizable volumes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "7.Define non-mobilizable volumes"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Residual volume (VR): volume of air that remains in the lung after"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "forced expiration =1.2 - 1.5L"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Functional residual capacity (CRF): this is the volume of air that remains"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "into the lung after normal expiration. CRF=ERV+VR"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Total lung capacity (CPT): this is the volume of air contained in the"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "lungs after forced inspiration. CPT=CV+VR =ERV+VRI+Vt+VR= 5,500 ml."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "?"
        }
      ]
    },
